{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788491815,"nonce":"bCwfhAogf5CpxLez6KU9AoxVyOM=","title":"Honest instruments: ok means what you asked for happened","message":"Part of the cockpit round, b4adee2. Design: RUNS/openrun-20260902/audit/COCKPIT.md\n§How it stays honest and §Where it lives (the two rulings it changes). The\naudit's themes T0, T1, T2, T3, T8, T9.\n\nWHAT\n\nFive rules for the verb surface, each a change to shipped behaviour. They are\nhere rather than in the screen spec because they are about every reply, not\nabout the one reply that is the screen.\n\n1. `ok` means the thing you asked for happened. A verb that did not — data.ok\n   false, changed 0 when a change was asked, order_effect gone, accepted 0, a\n   clamped or lapsed line — returns ok:false with class refused and its detail\n   in the error block. This run's instances (themes.md T1): `build` refused by\n   a blocked interaction spot and read as a success, costing about one in-game\n   day with no research bench; `trade-start` that started nothing;\n   `carry` whose order the think-tree discarded; `bill-set` changed 0 four\n   times; `zone add` landing beside the pile; `alert-mute` muting what it was\n   asked to unmute; `flick` changed 0 rejected 1; `threat-pardon` reporting\n   success with refused_count 0 when every pardon lapsed (fee81b2). The agent\n   wrote its own wrapper to surface data.ok within an hour of the run starting;\n   that wrapper is what the mod should be.\n\n2. A stray key is refused on any verb that mutates differently when that key\n   is missing. The 7382bdd ruling of 2026-09-01 refuses strays on three fixture\n   verbs and reports them everywhere else; this run measured the report: read\n   zero times in 52 envelopes (T0). It also found five more verbs whose default\n   mutates: `posture` (no pawns means all seven — the #2 link in the wipe),\n   `alert-mute` (no op means mute), `carry` (no destination means a default\n   one), `trade-start` (no trader means a default one), and `build` (a dropped\n   dry_run means a real blueprint; eleven consecutive calls wrote `dry-run`).\n   The mechanism is RefuseStray's message-only list, extended to those five and\n   to place-layout and zone for dry_run; the detection stays the read log. And\n   hyphenated argument keys are read as underscored at the poller, since no verb\n   reads a hyphenated key and the op names themselves are hyphenated.\n\n3. A capped read says so first. `things`, `zones` and a pawn's conditions put\n   \"20 of 76 shown\" in the first line of the reply; `hediff_cap` becomes an\n   argument (it is a constant today, and for one augmented colonist every real\n   bionic sat below it for the rest of the run); and a rollup never reports one\n   coordinate for many things — the `at` field that read \"6 mini-turrets at\n   [85,79]\" while two stood fifteen cells away. Stated in DESIGN's words: a\n   capped read cannot be used to verify a change made across the whole set;\n   the screen's full count is what verifies.\n\n4. The correction rides in the error path. Refusals already name the legal set\n   nearly every time; keep that. `verbs` gains, per verb, the argument keys it\n   has read on this bench — derived from the VerbArgs read log across the\n   session and the selftest, never declared, so there is no second source of\n   truth (the rejection of the per-verb whitelist stands). This is 5fd6dde's\n   discoverability without its whitelist.\n\n5. The plural form. `build` takes a list of placements; `orders` takes a list\n   of things; `nearest` honours its limit. 198 bursts of four or more identical\n   ops covered 53% of everything issued this run, and in eleven of the fourteen\n   largest the argument count equals the burst length: not retries, the absence\n   of a plural form. The client-side loop stays for the ragged tail.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n\n- Each instance under rule 1 has a bench or fakebench check where the old\n  envelope said ok:true and the new one says ok:false, class refused, with the\n  same detail the inner field used to carry.\n- posture without pawns, alert-mute without op, carry without to, trade-start\n  without trader, and build with `dry-run` are each refused before mutating,\n  naming the key and the fix.\n- `build {dry-run:true}` and `build {dry_run:true}` are the same call.\n- things --def MineableSteel with 134 on the map: the first line is \"30 of 134\n  shown\"; --detail_cap 200 shows all; the reply for six turrets lists six\n  positions.\n- pawn --hediff_cap 80 shows 40 conditions on a pawn with 40.\n- rwa verbs prints, for every verb the selftest exercises, the keys it read.\n- Thirty build calls become one, and thirty results come back in one envelope.\n\nABSORBS\n\nfee81b2 (rule 1), 5fd6dde (rule 4). Left open beside this: 7e8c969 (its\nsilver-row arithmetic is its own bug), 253c694 (collision semantics), 61794cd\n(bleed-out clock, in progress), e440676 (land it), 5697725 (the README's\nlandmark form).","files":null}]}